time required: 30 minutes
alternative_name: Broccoli Pasta
ingredient_count: 13
---

Chop fresh @broccoli florets{4%cups}(fresh or frozen, chopped) into small florets. If using frozen, let it stand out a few minutes, then give it a quick coarse chop. Measure and set aside.

Set a large #colander in the #sink with a #glass mug in the center of the #colander (so you don't forget to grab some pasta water before draining!). Bring a large #pot of water to a boil. Generously salt the water (I add @salt{2%teaspoons}), then cook @rotini pasta{3%9-ounce cups}(uncooked) according to package instructions—minus 1 minute. Two minutes before draining time, add broccoli. Right before draining, use #mug to remove a big scoop of pasta water (set aside) and drain the pasta. Don't rinse under cool water.

Meanwhile, in a large #pan (that will need to fit the pasta and broccoli), heat the @unsalted butter{2%tablespoons}. Once melted, add @garlic{2%teaspoons}(minced) and all seasonings: @Italian seasoning{1%teaspoon}, @onion powder{1/2%teaspoon}, @garlic powder{1/2%teaspoon}, and @?dried thyme{1/2%teaspoon}. Season with @salt{1/4%teaspoon} and @pepper{1/4%teaspoon}. Cook until golden, stirring constantly, about ~{30%seconds}. Pour in 1/2 cup @reduced-sodium chicken broth{1%cup}; it should sizzle and boil. Scrape up any browned bits off the #pan. Once this broth mostly evaporates, add the other 1/2 cup. Stir.

Add in @heavy cream{1%cup} and @Parmesan cheese{3/4%cup}. Stir to mix. Simmer over medium heat, stirring occasionally, ~{3-5%minutes} or until sauce thickens and slightly reduces. The sauce shouldn't boil—reduce heat and stir more frequently if needed.

> See note 1 for Parmesan cheese recommendations.

Once you have a thick and creamy sauce, add drained pasta and broccoli. Use #tongs to toss ingredients into cream sauce until sauce thickens and nicely coats the pasta, ~{1-2%minutes}. If sauce is too thick, slowly add in set-aside pasta water. Taste and adjust, adding more salt/pepper to taste. Add @?lemon{1}(zested) zest to taste if desired.

Serve immediately. Top individual plates with a touch more Parmesan if you like and @?fresh parsley{}(finely chopped). Add @?red pepper flakes{} and a squeeze of fresh lemon juice to individual plates as desired. Enjoy immediately! Pasta is best enjoyed right after being tossed!